.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt SLEEP 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sleep
.Nd delay for a whole number of seconds
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Delay for the requested number of seconds, then exit.
The operand must be a whole decimal number from 0 through 4294967295.
A zero duration returns immediately.
The delay uses the existing monotonic kernel timer.
Scheduling may make it longer than requested.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
This is the unmodified sbase 0.1 implementation from the pinned archive;
see
.Xr sbase 7 .
Fractional durations, unit suffixes, and multiple duration operands are
not accepted.
ABSD has no POSIX signal delivery or interrupted-duration reporting;
the shell's documented session interruption applies.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after a valid duration completes, nonzero for invalid options or operands.
Successful execution produces no output.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sleep 1
/bin/echo before; sleep 1; /bin/echo after
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
.Xr uptime 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
